1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,240
That-That's okay.
I can infer from context.

2
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:07,420
Hey, Raj, you wanna see a new
magic trick I been working on?

3
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:08,640
Eh, Howard.

4
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:11,740
(Sheldon:)If I may interject here
with a piece of friendly advice.

5
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:15,580
(Sheldon:)Is working on magic tricks, really
how you want to spend your time?

6
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:19,380
Uh, granted,
you're just an engineer, but...

7
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:23,860
(Sheldon:)That doesn't mean you might
not someday build a geegaw

8
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,090
(Sheldon:)or a thingamabob that

9
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:29,660
that may get you a "thank you" in someone
else's Nobel Prize acceptance speech.

10
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,520
(Raj:)Is the trick making him disappear?

11
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,180
(Raj:)Sure, let's see it.

12
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,080
(Sheldon:)Here.
Shuffle these.

13
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:44,310
(Priya:)Okay.

14
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:47,340
(Howard:)Now spread them out on the table.
Face down.

15
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,330
(Howard:)Pick one.
Look at it.

16
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:50,550
(Priya:)Okay.

17
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:52,550
(Howard:)Now remember your card.
Put it back in the deck.

18
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:54,480
(Sheldon:)Is it any wonder
he doesn't have a doctorate?

19
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,430
Now remind me,
what's your birthday?

20
00:00:58,450 --> 00:00:59,650
(Raj:)October sixth.

21
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:03,100
(Howard:)Okay, October is the tenth month.

22
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:07,660
So 10-- one plus zero
is one plus six is seven.

23
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,880
(Howard:)Turn over the seventh card.

24
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:13,740
(Raj:)How about that!

25
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:14,960
But, is that your card?

26
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:16,470
(Raj:)Yes. It is.
Very cool!

27
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:20,190
Oh it's not cool.

28
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:25,080
(Sheldon:)It's a childish trick, designed
to confuse and intrigue simpletons.

29
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:27,300
(Sheldon:)How'd you do it?

30
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:30,350
(Howard:)A magician never reveals his secrets.

31
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,200
(Howard:)But surely a future
Nobel Prize winner can figure it out.

32
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:36,650
(Sheldon:)Fine.

33
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:37,870
(Sheldon:)Give me a second.

34
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:44,910
(Howard:)You ever notice when he thinks
real hard it smells like bacon?

35
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:49,950
- Oh hey!
- Sorry! Oop!

36
00:01:58,220 --> 00:02:04,020
(Leonard:)Check it out.
I just got contacts.

